mod module_builtin_name_nameres;

// A name of core taken for a name of this module's own. Every module imports
// core with a wildcard, and core folds Option and Result in and, with
// 'pub use', their variants, so each is a name of every module; two different
// things under one name collide ("One declaration by two routes",
// doc/design/names-and-namespaces.md). The core import is written nowhere, so
// the collision is reported at the other binding, the one the source can
// change, and says where the name came from. It was once reported at an empty
// line in a file called "init", the compiler's own starting point, and said
// only that a folded name must be unique.
//
// The modules named after one are Option.cone, a one-file submodule, whose
// name is refused twice at its 'mod' line: once in its own namespace, which
// holds its own name, and once in this one's, which holds its submodule's.
// And sister.cone imports it, so its binding of the name is refused there too.
//
// Name resolution: the core import's names are folded in the fold passes.

struct Some {               //~ ErrorDupName:8 "Some is already a name of this module, and core, which every module imports"
}
